WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.900
Eye for eye, tooth for tooth.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.370
To many people, that
sounds like pure revenge.

3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.690
Yet many readers see this
ancient law as a limit:

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.050
a penalty that fits
the crime, and no more.

5
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.490
Today, a judge must also
think about the future:

6
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.400
about other people,
and about the offender.

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:24.030
So when someone breaks the law, what
should punishment actually achieve?

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.300
In this mission, you'll meet
the main aims of punishment,

9
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.790
with the strengths and weaknesses of each.

10
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.890
Then you'll see which Bible
passages Christians use,

11
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.850
and why Christians weigh
these aims differently.

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: work out what
punishment should achieve,

13
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.950
and why believers weigh
the aims differently.
